---
// Teaching page: the programme told as a case, the Think First method with
// an annotated worksheet, our promises, the four modules, and where we teach.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageTop from '../components/PageTop.astro';
import OnThisPage from '../components/OnThisPage.astro';
import Case from '../components/Case.astro';
import Steps from '../components/Steps.astro';
import Annotated from '../components/Annotated.astro';
import Gallery from '../components/Gallery.astro';
import MarginNote from '../components/MarginNote.astro';
import '../styles/pages/teaching.css';
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import { facts, showSamples } from '../data/facts';
import { getLangFromUrl, ui } from '../i18n';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const f = facts;

// The four teaching modules (src/content/programs/; drafts excluded).
const modules = await Promise.all(
  (await getCollection('programs'))
    .filter((m) => !m.data.draft)
    .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
    .map(async (m) => ({ ...m.data, Body: (await render(m)).Content }))
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Teaching"
  pageClass="page-teaching"
  description="Free tutoring for primary school children from underprivileged families in Hong Kong. 350 children taught across 7 schools by 43 trained student tutors, and 86% have moved up at least one class band since 2024."
>
  <PageTop vertical="教學">
    <h1>Free tutoring where children try first and ask the AI second.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Our student tutors teach primary school children from underprivileged families across Hong Kong.
      Every subject is paired with AI, so the children leave with a free, patient study partner they can
      keep using.
    </p>
    <OnThisPage
      items={[
        { href: '#how-it-started', label: 'How it started' },
        { href: '#think-first', label: 'Think First' },
        { href: '#promises', label: 'Promises' },
        { href: '#modules', label: 'Modules' },
        { href: '#sample-lesson', label: 'Sample lesson' },
        { href: '#where-we-teach', label: 'Where we teach' },
      ]}
    />
  </PageTop>

  <!-- The programme, told the way we tell every piece of work -->
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="how-it-started">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Case
        id="how-it-started"
        title="Why we teach, and what's changed."
        noticed={{
          date: '2023',
          text: "In Hong Kong, extra help after school usually costs money. Families who can pay for tutoring do, and families who can't watch their children fall behind. A patient AI tutor could change that, but only for children shown how to use it well.",
        }}
        did={{
          date: '2024/2026',
          text: `We trained ${f.tutors.value} secondary-school tutors and taught ${f.children.value} children four modules (maths, English, economics and science) in ${f.schools.word.en} schools, every lesson built on Think First.`,
        }}
        changed={{
          dateLabel: `Since ${f.bandUp.since}`,
          status: 'changed',
          figure: `${f.bandUp.value}${f.bandUp.unit}`,
          text: 'of our students have moved up at least one class band.',
        }}
      >
        <Fragment slot="changed-note">
          <MarginNote label="About that number." id="results">
            We don't claim it as ours alone. Teachers, families and the students themselves did the work.
            But it's the number we hold ourselves to.
          </MarginNote>
          {
            showSamples && f.bandUp.method.sample && (
              <MarginNote label="How we count it.">
                <span class="sample-tag" data-sample>{ui[lang].sample}</span>
                {f.bandUp.method.en}
              </MarginNote>
            )
          }
          {!f.bandUp.method.sample && <MarginNote label="How we count it.">{f.bandUp.method.en}</MarginNote>}
        </Fragment>
      </Case>

      <figure class="quote">
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            We went to Ling To expecting to spend the session convincing a room of children that AI and
            current affairs had anything to do with them. We were wrong. They weren't uninterested; nobody
            had ever given them the chance. Within an hour they were arguing about whether an algorithm
            could be fair. Curiosity was never what was missing. Access was.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption>One of our tutors, after a session at Ho Man Tin Ling To Catholic School</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="think-first">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="think-first">Every lesson follows the same four steps.</h2>
        <p>
          A tool is only as useful as a child's ability to use it well. A child who asks AI for the answer
          learns nothing. A child who tries first, asks for a hint, and then explains the answer in their
          own words learns more than they would have on their own. Teaching that difference is what our
          tutors do. We call it Think First.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Steps
        items={[
          { name: 'Attempt', text: 'Children try the problem on their own first.' },
          { name: 'Ask', text: 'They ask the AI for a hint or a check, never for the answer.' },
          { name: 'Check', text: "They compare the AI's reply with their own work and spot the differences." },
          { name: 'Explain', text: 'With the AI switched off, they explain the answer in their own words.' },
        ]}
      />

      <p class="sheet-intro">
        This is the worksheet from one of our lessons, where children compare two characters from a game
        they play, then argue which is better.
      </p>
      <Annotated
        notes={[
          'They read the numbers from their own game, so the data is theirs.',
          "The surprise: the faster character usually wins. One number on its own doesn't tell you much.",
          "One honest sentence for the other side. It's the same rule we use in every proposal.",
        ]}
      />

      <p class="closing-line">
        If a child can explain it without the AI, they've learned it. If they can't, we go back a step.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What schools and families can count on -->
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="promises">
    <div class="wrap rail">
      <div class="rail-head">
        <h2 id="promises">What schools and families can count on.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="promise-list">
        <li>Tutors always teach with a member of school or centre staff in the room.</li>
        <li>We don't collect children's personal data.</li>
        <li>We only use AI tools the partner school has approved.</li>
        <li>Teaching is always free.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="modules">
    <div class="wrap rail">
      <div class="rail-head">
        <h2 id="modules">Four school subjects, each with AI as a study partner.</h2>
        <p>
          We don't teach AI as a separate topic. Our tutors are secondary school students who finish AFG's
          training before they teach, and they work in small groups so every child gets attention.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="module-list">
        {
          modules.map((m) => (
            <li class="module">
              <h3>{m.title}</h3>
              <p>{m.summary}</p>
              {m.why && (
                <p class="module-why">
                  <b>How it helps:</b> {m.why}
                </p>
              )}
              <details>
                <summary>More about this module</summary>
                <div class="prose">
                  <m.Body />
                </div>
              </details>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="sample-lesson">
    <div class="wrap rail">
      <div class="rail-head">
        <h2 id="sample-lesson">A lesson, start to finish.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          <strong>Bigger isn't better:</strong> a 60-minute lesson for P5–P6 using maths and English, with
          2 tutors for every 8–10 students. We've published it so schools can see how a lesson is put
          together before they invite us in.
        </p>
        <p><a class="textlink" href="/teaching/sample-lesson">The full lesson plan</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="where-we-teach">
    <div class="wrap rail">
      <div class="rail-head">
        <h2 id="where-we-teach">Where we teach.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="prose">
          We teach in primary schools including <strong>Ho Man Tin Ling To Catholic School</strong> and{' '}
          <strong>Kennedy Town School</strong>, and with our community partners{' '}
          <strong>St. Barnabas' Home &amp; Society</strong> and <strong>10% Organisation</strong>.
        </p>
        <div class="place-gallery">
          <Gallery
            photos={[
              {
                name: 'teaching-ai-tools.jpg',
                alt: 'Two tutors introduce what an AI assistant can do: find information, break down hard questions, and help with writing.',
                caption: 'Introducing what an AI assistant can do, at Ho Man Tin Ling To Catholic School.',
              },
              {
                name: 'teaching-english-careers.jpg',
                alt: 'Two tutors run the English module, with a slide on how English opens career doors in healthcare, trade, technology, and tourism.',
                caption: 'The English module.',
              },
              {
                name: 'teaching-exploring-interests.jpg',
                alt: 'A tutor shows pupils how to use AI to explore their own interests, from dinosaurs to space to music.',
                caption: 'Using AI to explore your own interests.',
              },
            ]}
          />
        </div>

        <h3 class="place-h">With Victoria Shanghai Academy</h3>
        <p class="prose">
          Alongside our work in primary schools, we run sessions with Victoria Shanghai Academy for young
          people from the local community.
        </p>
        <dl class="years">
          <div>
            <dt>2024–25</dt>
            <dd>
              Showing students how AI can be used in their own community: what the tools are good at, and
              how to use them for something that actually helps.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>2025–26</dt>
            <dd>
              Teaching local children what AI can make better, and how to spot and avoid the ways it gets
              misused.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <div class="place-gallery">
          <Gallery
            photos={[
              {
                name: 'vsa-2025-26-poster.jpg',
                alt: 'Students build posters setting out a problem, an AI solution, and how it would be implemented.',
                caption: 'Students plan how AI could help with a problem in their community, 2025–26.',
              },
              {
                name: 'vsa-2024-25-group.jpg',
                alt: 'Tutors and students at the close of the 2024–25 sessions, in front of a slide thanking everyone for joining.',
                caption: 'The end of the 2024–25 sessions.',
              },
              {
                name: 'vsa-2025-26-cohort.jpg',
                alt: 'The 2025–26 group of students and tutors together in the classroom.',
                caption: 'Students and tutors, 2025–26.',
              },
            ]}
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
